{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178976-cryptocurrency-and-the-vas","id":1178976,"title":"Cryptocurrency and the VAs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-24T15:38:25-08:00","id":1178976,"title":"Cryptocurrency and the VAs","content":"So, I think that the rise of cryptocurrencies in real life presents some neat opportunities within Mage. I think it's a neat focus for VAs and a potential plot hook to start a cold war between the Adepts and the Syndicate.<br /> <br /> Anybody else see plot potential here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T15:53:00-08:00","id":1178978,"title":"","content":"I imagine it being something a VA in Japan was working on, partially a personal project of coding currency into existence, and then suddenly they struck upon something which chimes with the consensus. How? Because the syndicate were working on the very same thing, a little thing called Primal Utility. Had the syndicate not set the stage, it would have been vulgar beyond use, but now the VAs had a way to magic up money in a coincidental manner outside the control of the syndicate. They told a bunch of guys online and soon the digital web was awash with the stuff.<br /> <br /> When the syndicate bosses found out, they would not have been happy. Some punk hackers taking the theories they had spent literal millions developing, driving into the consensus, and maintaining control being used to undermine that very control.<br /> <br /> It had to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T15:54:25-08:00","id":1178980,"title":"","content":"With all these ups and down, which are very violent in terms of asset pricing, I'd say that cryptocurrency are still very paradoxical. Market corrections are still too strong.<br /> <br /> They might be a new experiment from the Syndicate in their eternal search of new profit avenue to keep the Technocracy afloat. Maybe the limitations and bans that governments and central banks are rising to oppose bitcoins are just the NWO trying to limit a flow of money and power that would be too free (Syndicate loves free-market, unbound by any rules, but for control freaks like the NWO the whole idea of a cryptocurrency would be anathema).<br /> <br /> Maybe the hackers attack on the various cryptocurrency exchange platform like Mt.Gox are a new strategy of the Virtual adepts that want to crush the new money avenue of the Syndicate.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T16:21:11-08:00","id":1178989,"title":"","content":"Cryptocurrency is very much something that the Syndicate stole from the VAs not the other way. I mean something that starts out as a neat experiment with technology and leads to &quot;number one source of black market transfers&quot; should probably tell you who's running the thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T19:31:52-08:00","id":1179059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178976-cryptocurrency-and-the-vas?p=1178989#post1178989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cryptocurrency is very much something that the Syndicate stole from the VAs not the other way. I mean something that starts out as a neat experiment with technology and leads to &quot;number one source of black market transfers&quot; should probably tell you who's running the thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how the VAs would see it, certainly. Though the syndicate would have ways of proving they came up with it first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T19:36:32-08:00","id":1179060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178976-cryptocurrency-and-the-vas?p=1178989#post1178989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cryptocurrency is very much something that the Syndicate stole from the VAs not the other way. I mean something that starts out as a neat experiment with technology and leads to &quot;number one source of black market transfers&quot; should probably tell you who's running the thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let\u2019s be fair though, a lot of things the Trads do are criminal and have to be kept untraceable by governmental and corporate authorities that the Union is woven through.<br /> <br /> Not saying the Syndicate don\u2019t also use it! Anything that gives commerce more independency from the NWO is inherently a way for them to shift the power balance in the Union. But the Trads are steeped in criminal underworld dealings themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-24-2018, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T20:42:03-08:00","id":1179078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178976-cryptocurrency-and-the-vas?p=1179060#post1179060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let\u2019s be fair though, a lot of things the Trads do are criminal and have to be kept untraceable by governmental and corporate authorities that the Union is woven through.<br /> <br /> Not saying the Syndicate don\u2019t also use it! Anything that gives commerce more independency from the NWO is inherently a way for them to shift the power balance in the Union. But the Trads are steeped in criminal underworld dealings themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would say that the syndicate generally has greater power in organized Crime than the Traditions, as the current use of cryptocurrency is organized crime and political corruption that undermines the power of government in certain countries. This isn't to say the Trads are morally pure as the snow they just lack the influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T20:42:29-08:00","id":1179079,"title":"","content":"In fact, I could see the VAs inventing it as a way of avoiding Technocratic scrutiny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T20:50:57-08:00","id":1179082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178976-cryptocurrency-and-the-vas?p=1179079#post1179079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, I could see the VAs inventing it as a way of avoiding Technocratic scrutiny.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, or purely out of experimentation. That's why I was saying the VAs may have started it but its fully in the hands of the Syndicate right now. Its not an attack against them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T21:10:39-08:00","id":1179095,"title":"","content":"I'm saying that it's not in the hands of the Syndicate: as glamourweaver pointed out, the Syndicate does not have a monopoly on the black market; they just have a significant presence there. And crypto-currency is something that strikes me as inherently resistant, if not outright immune, to being controlled; by design, it can't be \u201cin the hands of\u201d <i>anyone</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T22:19:46-08:00","id":1179112,"title":"","content":"I can actually also see Cryptocurrencies being a Syndicate experiment of their own, with natural (independent and unconnected) VA involvement in the process because of the digital nature of it all;<br /> The Syndicate's big spiel is worth and value, and like any other Tradition or Convention they are not inert in their development - except that previous experiments and overzealous application of principles in their case were reasons for stock crashes, economic deflation, and..well, Market Correction on a global, massive scale. Bad for everybody involved, and resons for termination of multiple Syndicate members.<br /> <br /> So why not experiment in a safer environment, courtesy of the VA's and the spread of the internet? Make it virtual, make any potential rises and falls much more 'localized' in the way that crashes and drops mostly affect crypto exchange and (heh) the GPU market prices instead of any global stock markets...and actually, bringing a Technocratic paradigms finally closer to the sleepers, much like the other conventions tend to do. Except in this case somebody actually, *actually* managed the neigh impossible - doing it with the esoteric and abstract concept of Primal Utility. If anything, cryptocurrencies might be an absolute stroke of genius for bringing the concept somewhat into their world. Value out of literally nothing tangible.<br /> Plus, the Syndicate is absolutely excellent at making use of the talents and natures of others, especially their foes, for fun and profit; I'm looking at you again, VA's. Keep up the good work in this.<br /> <br /> Naturally the NWO would be highly against such an uncontrolled and unregulated development, even if it is purely virtual; The 'Wild West' attitude of the Internet always was a big thorn in their side, with regulations, surveillance and control of the digital world increasing more and more in the NWO's wake; Naturally cryptocurrencies run afoul of that, so steps are in motion already - bans, regulations, tecnnologies to put surveillance onto previously touted 'Anonymous' transactions....the NWO would actually have a bigger problem with monetary development outside of Bank control than the Syndicate.<br /> In the end it might actually be as much of an experiment as a cold war of the Syndicate *against* the NWO, heh.<br /> <br /> I dunno, just a thought and different perspective <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> To add, I really don't see the whole thing as being alternatively possibly started by the VA's. Cryptocurrencies play right into the Syndicate's paradigm, and the whole argument of &quot;It's digital, thus must be VA&quot; seems kind of thin and clich\u00e9. Now ,it's true that they probably were heavily involved in some mining in the beginning, because cryptocurrencies were totally marketed (Oh, hey....) towards 'less regulations, freedom!', but one has to wonder about the plans behind that...<br /> <br /> Also, random thought, I can see the blockchain as well as the spirit of the algorithms as being this incredibly large, intricate, complex thing in the Digital Web, fortified with mechanisms throughout against metaphyiscal tampering...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 01-25-2018, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T01:03:05-08:00","id":1179133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178976-cryptocurrency-and-the-vas?p=1179095#post1179095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm saying that it's not in the hands of the Syndicate: as glamourweaver pointed out, the Syndicate does not have a monopoly on the black market; they just have a significant presence there. And crypto-currency is something that strikes me as inherently resistant, if not outright immune, to being controlled; by design, it can't be \u201cin the hands of\u201d <i>anyone</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would profoundly disagree. Much of the mechanics that is used for fighting the Ascension war especially in in a post pogrom world(social engineering for example) would be profoundly useful in manipulating and controlling cryptocurrencies. This is of course before having.. stuff like Entropy, Time and Primal Utility.<br /> <br /> Just alone being able to manipulate the ease of liquidation for bitcoin alone would give it profound control over it, which the Syndicate could readily do. The fact that it bitcoin has profound issues being used as a proper currency because of the difficulties in transferring it already points to a level of potential control if there were some sort of global monetary conspiracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T05:43:37-08:00","id":1179162,"title":"","content":"The Syndicate wants a cashless world with purely virtual transactions. However, I see in this thread that everyone seems to believe that they don't want these transactions to be &quot;controled&quot;. I disagree:<br /> <br /> Remember that they are all about Crowdfunding but against individual creators (or groups of creators). It's in their book, independant creators in the internet are the bane of the Syndicate, no matter how marketable they may become. The Syndicate WANTS to control Utility, free creators are untapped utility but Crowdfunding can be easily followed and controled by an institution (the ONG that organizes it). In the same vein, they will want to control the transactions, that's why they're Technocracy's bankers and financists. The Syndicate doesn't want transactions to be harder to follow.<br /> <br /> In the same vein, VA aren't engineers that don't want anything in the world but to experiment and enjoy intelectual bliss, they're hackers that are all about freedom, and doing things in a place that can't be controled by any power. They're the provervial cowboys that don't obey the rules.<br /> <br /> SO<br /> <br /> I think this is one of those odd times were the objectives of the VA and the Syndicate collude to some extent. Syndicate wants a cashless world with instant transactions (prefferably outside the control of goverments, but not outside the control of financial institutions). VA wants virtual everything outside all control. -&gt; Cryptocurrency it's born as the inevitable result of VA AND Syndicate Paradigms being active in the Consensus.<br /> <br /> Currently VA and the Syndicate are fighting viciously to control the stuff (and NWO it's trying to put it down), after all, we constantly see that: Economists and financial institutions everywhere that talk trash about the stuff (Syndicate). Countries ban it (NWO). Hackers stealing it (VA) - I can see the Syndicate trying to foster the more &quot;controled&quot; forms of criptocurrency (while still using the uncontroled ones to do illegal stuff), in the long run they want a world controled by the financial institutions they have fostered, while VA would be behind the more esoterinc and uncontrolable criptocurrency (up to the point having their own super elite cryptocoin that muggles can't use)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-25-2018, 08:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T04:43:42-08:00","id":1179485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178976-cryptocurrency-and-the-vas?p=1178989#post1178989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cryptocurrency is very much something that the Syndicate stole from the VAs not the other way. I mean something that starts out as a neat experiment with technology and leads to &quot;number one source of black market transfers&quot; should probably tell you who's running the thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean like dollars?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178976-cryptocurrency-and-the-vas?p=1179095#post1179095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm saying that it's not in the hands of the Syndicate: as glamourweaver pointed out, the Syndicate does not have a monopoly on the black market; they just have a significant presence there. And crypto-currency is something that strikes me as inherently resistant, if not outright immune, to being controlled; by design, it can't be \u201cin the hands of\u201d <i>anyone</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is probably the greatest advantage of the blockchain-maintained, open source, consensus-determined currency. Such design is today probably the closest analog to the ideal &quot;money&quot; that we can reach.<br /> <br /> Can't really control it, can't really counterfeit it, if by whatever reason you want out you can start your own and just have to convince people your idea is better, which on the long term will usually happen regardless of your persuasion if it actually is better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 01-26-2018, 07:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T15:29:37-08:00","id":1179642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178976-cryptocurrency-and-the-vas?p=1179485#post1179485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean like dollars?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes? No one questions that the Technocracy has its hands in all levels of governments.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is probably the greatest advantage of the blockchain-maintained, open source, consensus-determined currency. Such design is today probably the closest analog to the ideal &quot;money&quot; that we can reach.<br /> <br /> Can't really control it, can't really counterfeit it, if by whatever reason you want out you can start your own and just have to convince people your idea is better, which on the long term will usually happen regardless of your persuasion if it actually is better. </div> </div> </div>You CAN control it. The whole Cryptocurrency market lost the equivalent of 200 billion dollars during one day of sales based on government announcements. The ease of transfering it changes by time of day and how readily people are using it. Its also fairly unstable.<br /> <br /> So yeah if you value being able to use currency for its purpose Cryptocurrency is currently pretty damned bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T09:13:31-08:00","id":1179848,"title":"","content":"Well, duh. Of course anyone with sufficient amounts of money or control over others can generate wild swings. That's not the control I was talking about. I was talking about assuming control of its functions. Of its nature.<br /> <br /> But you want to talk about controlling exchange rates, let's talk about controlling exchange rates:<br /> A president, not a year ago, in a single day and with a single statement about an internal matter made that nation's currency lose over 2 trillion dollars via exchange devaluation.<br /> Also in a single day, based on panic from a single vote, another nation's currency lost nearly twice that much.<br /> <br /> Are you telling me that cryptos are bad because they can oscillate? Because they do oscillate? <i>Or because governments keep getting in the way</i>? Very different things, each of those reasons.<br /> <br /> You also speak of a currency's purpose.<br /> What is &quot;its purpose&quot;, Lian? There's more than one currency being talked about here, cryptos are a category. They are also made with different purposes in mind.<br /> <br /> Bitcoin and Dash are made for trade. Dash is faster, cheaper and more anonymous, while Bitcoin is more widely accepted. Bitcoin's system is harder to change, while Dash's adapts faster to whatever need may appear.<br /> Both Dash and Bitcoin (and many others) are cheaper and faster to trade, internationally, than trading through fiat currency banks (Some banks are trying to invent their own internal cryptocurrency to compete)<br /> Ripple promises to be a way to send money via a p2p exchange of &quot;roughly every money ever&quot;, fiat or crypto, and might actually work some day.<br /> Ethereum is a contract signing method so good a couple countries are working to adapt it as a replacement for notary offices and registries.<br /> <br /> <br /> Are you telling me they are all bad for the same reason?<br /> <br /> For trading, for example, did you know that its value is not very relevant? As long as there's enough of it to cover whatever sum you want to transfer, you can buy them, send over to someone else, and that someone else sells it for his own preferred currency. A process that, if you are in a hurry, doesn't take 10 minutes. Cryptos bad for small transactions, like bitcoin, won't be cheap unless you're trading at least a couple thousand dollars.<br /> Are you telling me such currency oscillates within 5 to 10 minutes that much?<br /> <br /> Or, maybe, have you heard of Future Trades? For any currency that tends to gain value over another Future Trades is a way to guarantee you'll get the value you want from whatever you took. Such method is made viable if whatever's being insured gains value more often than it loses within whatever timespan the trader can withstand.<br /> Fiat currency is dealt in future trades for as long as commerce exists. Gold too. Commodities. Anything can be sold under such method. Criptos are just the newest thing, and not knowing the solution to their problems doesn't mean that they don't exist, nor that they are worse than other forms of money.<br /> <br /> <br /> Criptocurrencies are the new thing, and are damn disruptive. Governments are losing control of their people's money by the day as those tecnologies improve.<br /> You want to be realistic? Criptos won't do much more for the next decade. Give them another and when you see it the whole world will be changed drastically, and quite likely to the better.<br /> <br /> Couldn't be more appealing to Virtual Adept stories if you tried.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now let's apply this knowledge to the game!<br /> <br /> Cryptocurrencies are so named because their core is cryptographic. Do you know anything that can ruin how cryptography works at our current day? One easy is quantum computing. A quantum processor has the potential to tear apart how cryptography works, and currencies are part of it.<br /> Of course, don't be too apocalyptic about it unless you truly extend it to everything ever: If you make something that lolnopes any cryptographic hurdle you'll not only take over all cryptocoins ever, you'll take over every system from everything connected to the internet, ever.<br /> <br /> I'd make, for example, magick that uses quantum processing to break unbreakable systems, but not necessarily fast, or widely applicable. You still need to go through the hoops. One codebreaker may be dependant on your own super duper mega blaster computer, opening up the possibility of leaving a trail.<br /> Another might only work in direct contact with the system to be breached.<br /> <br /> Probably the most interesting trait cryptocurrencies bring to the game is untraceability: Not all cryptos are truly untraceable, but they're all untraceable enough if they're built for it. Bitcoin, for example, doesn't give you anything unless you already have access to the source of a transaction. Merely reading it off the blockchain is useless.<br /> <br /> How do you breach that? How do you use that? How will the NWO handle this loss of control? How will the Syndicate cherish it? How do Adepts that work with that change the world?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 01-27-2018, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T14:29:15-08:00","id":1179938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> 