e made for trade. Dash is faster, cheaper and more anonymous, while Bitcoin is more widely accepted. Bitcoin's system is harder to change, while Dash's adapts faster to whatever need may appear.<br /> Both Dash and Bitcoin (and many others) are cheaper and faster to trade, internationally, than trading through fiat currency banks (Some banks are trying to invent their own internal cryptocurrency to compete)<br /> Ripple promises to be a way to send money via a p2p exchange of &quot;roughly every money ever&quot;, fiat or crypto, and might actually work some day.<br /> Ethereum is a contract signing method so good a couple countries are working to adapt it as a replacement for notary offices and registries.<br /> <br /> <br /> Are you telling me they are all bad for the same reason?<br /> <br /> For trading, for example, did you know that its value is not very relevant? As long as there's enough of it to cover whatever sum you want to transfer, you can buy them, send over to someone else, and that someone else sells it for his own preferred currency. A process that, if you are in a hurry, doesn't take 10 minutes. Cryptos bad for small transactions, like bitcoin, won't be cheap unless you're trading at least a couple thousand dollars.<br /> Are you telling me such currency oscillates within 5 to 10 minutes that much?<br /> <br /> Or, maybe, have you heard of Future Trades? For any currency that tends to gain value over another Future Trades is a way to guarantee you'll get the value you want from whatever you took. Such method is made viable if whatever's being insured gains value more often than it loses within whatever timespan the trader can withstand.<br /> Fiat currency is dealt in future trades for as long as commerce exists. Gold too. Commodities. Anything can be sold under such method. Criptos are just the newest thing, and not knowing the solution to their problems doesn't mean that they don't exist, nor that they are worse than other forms of money. </div> </div> </div>If the purpose of cryptocurrencies is meant to replace government backed currencies, then currently they just don't do that. The fact that they function as commodities is the issue. Yes Trading in Pounds/dollars/Yen/RNB is hard... but I can go and buy something with them. There are places these are accepted as mediums of exchange. Cryptocurrency right now has to be converted into a medium of exchange and this makes them difficult to use, its compounded as people invest in them making them even more difficult to use.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Criptocurrencies are the new thing, and are damn disruptive. Governments are losing control of their people's money by the day as those tecnologies improve.<br /> You want to be realistic? Criptos won't do much more for the next decade. Give them another and when you see it the whole world will be changed drastically, and quite likely to the better.<br /> <br /> Couldn't be more appealing to Virtual Adept stories if you tried. </div> </div> </div>Or the bubble will pop because people aren't treating them at all as a medium of exchange but rather as &quot;a super investment opportunity&quot; and then when that bubble explodes broad trust of the idea is shattered thus pushing people back towards a &quot;properly controlled eviroment&quot;<br /> <br /> YOU couldn't get more Syndicate if you tried!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now let's apply this knowledge to the game!<br /> <br /> Cryptocurrencies are so named because their core is cryptographic. Do you know anything that can ruin how cryptography works at our current day? One easy is quantum computing. A quantum processor has the potential to tear apart how cryptography works, and currencies are part of it.<br /> Of course, don't be too apocalyptic about it unless you truly extend it to everything ever: If you make something that lolnopes any cryptographic hurdle you'll not only take over all cryptocoins ever, you'll take over every system from everything connected to the internet, ever.<br /> <br /> I'd make, for example, magick that uses quantum processing to break unbreakable systems, but not necessarily fast, or widely applicable. You still need to go through the hoops. One codebreaker may be dependant on your own super duper mega blaster computer, opening up the possibility of leaving a trail.<br /> Another might only work in direct contact with the system to be breached.<br /> <br /> Probably the most interesting trait cryptocurrencies bring to the game is untraceability: Not all cryptos are truly untraceable, but they're all untraceable enough if they're built for it. Bitcoin, for example, doesn't give you anything unless you already have access to the source of a transaction. Merely reading it off the blockchain is useless.<br /> <br /> How do you breach that? How do you use that? How will the NWO handle this loss of control? How will the Syndicate cherish it? How do Adepts that work with that change the world? </div> </div> </div>Or the very untracability is what will drive people away from it, repeated horror stories of people having their whole cryptocurrency stolen annonymously, its a long term game by the Syndicate to make people more afraid of the Internet and push things into greater control by &quot;trusted corporations&quot; because for some reason people think banks are safe after the shenanigans they pulled in 2008...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T14:58:29-08:00","id":1179946,"title":"","content":"Horrible as a medium of exchange. Except that it isn't, you ignored my argument there. Bitcoin is, today, THE best way to exchange large sums of money quick, safely and internationally.<br /> <br /> You say that because some new tech that arrived this decade hasn't &quot;replaced the old one&quot; it means its a failure. And you ignore that there are places where it DID replace the old one.<br /> You can't see a single drop without calling it a bubble, despite the fact this behavior matches the past expectations to the point there are memes about how bitcoin's price keeps crashing up.<br /> <br /> Fads rise and fall, and currencies are no different. People use the money that serves them best, and that isn't going to be discovered quickly (or even remain constant). But you refuse to acknowledge that money can be used for trade just because the headlines blare apocalyptic news.<br /> You see money with a trait that protects the fruits of your labor from having to answer to an entity pointing a gun to your head and you call it a bad thing!<br /> <br /> The NWO has you right where they want <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 01-27-2018, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T20:08:41-08:00","id":1180034,"title":"","content":"I'm actually using the Conspiracy theory that a rogue AI is actually the inventor of Bitcoin in my Mage story. This AI, known as MEDICI (Massively Evolved Distributed &amp; Interlaced Computer Intelligence) even has the Technocracy worried and afraid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23654-drunkenuraak","name":"DrunkenUraak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}